==============================================================================
DSH Bot: a modified version of DS Bot
==============================================================================

DSH Bot (https://github.com/MoLi-MoChou/dsh-bot) is DS Bot
(https://github.com/Fei2411/DeepSeek-Bot @ ae63b45, Apache-2.0, by Fei2411
and the DS Bot contributors), imported unchanged and then modified. Every
change is listed here (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)); code changes carry a
"DSH Bot patch" comment.

  1. Name and look: the app is "Moon Bot" in every language (appId
     com.molimochou.moonbot, artifact names Moon-Bot-*, Linux executable
     moon-bot, data folder ~/.moon-bot, releases and links point at
     MoLi-MoChou/moon-bot). It was called "DSH Bot" and then "Mochou" (莫愁);
     their data folders (~/.dsh-bot, ~/.mochou) and settings (DSH_BOT_*,
     MOCHOU_*) still work. The plugin folder ds-bot/ is now core/ and its
     package is moon-bot-core. DS Bot's whale is replaced by Moon Bot's own
     lilac moon sprite, as the Main Bot's avatar and in the app icon, and a
     "Moon" theme (the default) joins DeepSeek, Claude and Grok Bot.
  2. Slim product (core/src/client/lean.js): group chats, scheduled /
     automation tasks, the "Add DSH Agent" entry and the classic Agent mode
     switch are not offered (menus, settings pages, details drawer). The code
     stays; one flag brings each back.
  3. Work steps (core/src/client/work-process.js): DS Bot's inline thinking
     row is replaced by one line per finished turn, "已工作 Xs · N 步"; it opens
     a side panel with the turn's thinking, tool calls (input, output) and
     replies in order.
  4. Cards discoverable: starter chips over a fresh chat's composer
     (core/src/client/starters.js), one prompt line that maps comparison,
     to-do and "give me options" asks to show_view cards
     (core/src/host/prompt.js), and matching replies in the dev mock model.
  5. Updates: the Linux AppImage updates itself like the Windows installer;
     releases are GitHub pre-releases (allowPrerelease); Settings > About shows
     the app's own updater (check, download progress, restart to update) via
     the app bridge (app/src/updates.mjs, main.mjs, preload.cjs, about.js); a
     portable Windows exe is added and points at the releases page.
  6. Data: a new install keeps its data in ~/.dsh-bot (DS Bot: ~/.ds-bot).
     A test feed (DS_BOT_UPDATE_URL) asks one range per request.
  7. Checks: scripts/scan.mjs no longer flags "DSH Bot" / dsh-bot (DS Bot's
     former name, this fork's name); test.yml checks the DSH Bot installer and
     has no macOS package or Docker job (neither is shipped).
  8. CI: .github/workflows/desktop.yml replaces release.yml (no npm publish);
     a v* tag builds Windows + Linux, runs check-packed, and publishes a
     pre-release with latest.yml, the .blockmap and latest-linux.yml.
  9. Lean tools: under the slim product the Bots' own chats also lose the group
     and schedule tools (core/src/shared/lean.js, host/tools.ts guard) and
     the prompt rules about them (host/prompt.js). DSH's Automation tasks panel,
     scheduler, schedule tool and product-telemetry export are switched off in
     core/cordis.patch.yml.
 10. Size: the Office-to-PDF engine (LibreOfficeKit) is not packaged; the app
     downloads it once after install from npm (mirror fallback), checks its
     sha512 from the lockfile and unpacks it under the user data folder
     (app/src/engines.mjs; Settings > About shows its state). zod is deduped by
     an npm override; Electron keeps the zh-CN and en-US locales; source maps,
     type declarations, test folders and the musl libvips are left out; the
     optional DSH bundles the slim product does not offer (inspector, agent
     team, ralph, badge skill, CoT translation, plugin market, worktree) are
     dropped (app/scripts/prune.mjs, electron-builder.yml).
 11. Linux sandbox: the AppImage adds --no-sandbox when the kernel or AppArmor
     forbids unprivileged user namespaces (app/src/sandbox.mjs);
     DSH_BOT_SANDBOX=1 keeps the sandbox.
 12. About lists "基于 DS Bot" with a link to the upstream project. The dev mock
     model answers "提权" in a Bot's own chat with a full-access shell request.
 13. Web mode (app/src/web.mjs): the same UI served by the Node host behind a
     password page, `npm run web` and a Dockerfile. Themes are DeepSeek, Claude
     and Grok Bot (light and dark). Motion and chat details follow open-claude-ui.

